<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TEMPLATE. `{{VERSION}}` is filled by packaging/render.mjs.

  This package DOWNLOADS the installer from the GitHub Release rather than
  embedding it, which is why there is no `VERIFICATION.txt` here: that file is
  Chocolatey's requirement for packages that ship binaries inside the nupkg, so
  a moderator can confirm they match upstream. A download package proves the
  same thing with the checksums in tools/chocolateyinstall.ps1, and those are
  what the moderators check instead — see packaging/README.md.

  What it downloads is the WiX MSI, which installs PER-MACHINE and therefore
  needs an elevated shell. `choco install` normally is one; the reasoning, and
  what it costs a non-admin, is at the top of tools/chocolateyinstall.ps1 and
  in packaging/README.md. The description below says so too, because the
  package page is where somebody finds out before they run it rather than
  after.
-->
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>kavka</id>
    <version>{{VERSION}}</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka/tree/main/packaging/chocolatey</packageSourceUrl>
    <owners>sahilhirani</owners>

    <title>Kavka</title>
    <authors>Sahil Hirani</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka</projectUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sahilhirani/kavka/main/apps/desktop/src-tauri/icons/128x128.png</iconUrl>
    <copyright>Copyright (C) 2026 Sahil Hirani</copyright>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <projectSourceUrl>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka</projectSourceUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka/blob/main/docs/FEATURES.md</docsUrl>
    <bugTrackerUrl>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka/issues</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>kafka apache-kafka kafka-client streaming devops developer-tools foss</tags>
    <summary>A fast, fully open-source desktop client for Apache Kafka.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Kavka is a desktop client for Apache Kafka for Windows and macOS.

* **Browse and search** — streaming search across a whole topic with CEL
  filters, Avro/Protobuf/JSON Schema decoding through Schema Registry, and a
  payload inspector.
* **Operate** — consumer group lag and offset resets, ACLs, client quotas,
  partition reassignment, Kafka Connect, Schema Registry management.
* **Monitor** — lag history, throughput charts, alert rules with Windows
  notifications and webhooks.
* **Power tools** — SQL over topics, cross-cluster copy and diff, DLQ
  workflows, an MCP server so an AI assistant can read your clusters, and
  WebAssembly custom decoders.

Every feature is free — no paid tiers, no licence keys, no server component.
Connection passwords go to Windows Credential Manager, and nothing about your
clusters leaves the machine.

Licensed AGPL-3.0: free for personal and commercial use, and a modified Kavka
that is distributed or offered as a service must publish its source.

**Installs per-machine.** This package downloads Kavka's MSI, so it needs an
elevated shell — which is what `choco install` normally runs in, and what a
fleet tool always does. For a per-user install on your own laptop with no
admin rights, use `winget install SahilHirani.Kavka` or the `.exe` on the
releases page.
    ]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/sahilhirani/kavka/releases/tag/v{{VERSION}}</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
